& [ConceptualModel] separates governance, events, derivations, and claims
  + FormationRevision is one prospective authority generation
  + ScannerObservationPolicy is the unchanged scanner profile 0.1 contract
  + ActualAcquisition is a future authority-bearing physical event
  + AcquisitionLineage is the retained ancestry of one complete event
  + CausalOrder relates first completion to second start
  + CommonScope states exact equality of every declared scope coordinate
  + InventoryCarrier is one complete supplied structural derivation bound to an acquisition only under future authority
  + OrderedDigestCarrier is one canonical sequence commitment retaining its full carrier ancestry
  + ReconciliationResult is current pure Equal or Different with complete operand lineage
  + InventoryConsistencyEvidence is a current claim-grade vocabulary
  + TopologyReceipt is a pure representation of bounded claims
  + IssuanceProof and ConsumptionDecision are future distinct authority-bearing records

& [AuthorityIdentities] are generation separated
  + [prior_formation_signature] is 040c8eb3-4c55-42c7-b731-f1223fb6b05f
  + [replacement_formation_signature] is absent until complete artifact-bound SJS
  + [machine_forms_signature] is c681b74d-7543-43be-96a1-a8ccb89181fb
  + [topology_forms_signature] is 1edee945-9957-41d7-bd17-0765ec54f5cb
  + [assembly_signature] is 9c92f968-054a-42de-a27f-90925bb5081e
  + [digest_signature] is 63c58b74-0eb9-4ab8-9c95-4bfe3bb92af8
  + [reconciliation_signature] is a763535f-3b13-4539-9aba-d74f09e3de5c
  + no signature identity is interchangeable with another role

& [ProfileIdentities] are exact
  + [scanner_observation_profile] is cantor-windows-candidate-topology/0.1
  + [phase3_machine_forms_profile] is cantor-phase3-machine-forms/0.2
  + [topology_forms_profile] is cantor-phase3-topology-forms/0.3
  + [topology_receipt_profile] is cantor-phase3-topology-receipt/0.3
  + [revision_profile] is cantor-phase3-topology-scanner-formation-consistency-evidence-reconciliation/0.1
  + representation profile changes do not imply scanner behavior changes
  + formation revision identity does not imply runtime profile availability

& [AcquisitionIdentityModel] is conceptual and exact
  + one AcquisitionIdentity names one future actual producer event
  + identity must be stable within the future issuer proof
  + first and second identities must differ
  + identity is not a digest, nonce, tick, path, operand index, or receipt hash
  + this revision does not select its byte representation
  + later M2C source must select bounded representation and collision domain

& [AcquisitionLineageModel] is independently complete
  + each lineage references one acquisition identity and one authorized producer identity
  + each lineage binds exact scanner policy and common scope values
  + each lineage records completion under the full traversal contract
  + each lineage retains root observation and complete entry derivation ancestry
  + each lineage retains one assembly carrier and one ordered digest carrier
  + one lineage never satisfies missing fields of the other
  + no bare digest or mutable shared pointer is a lineage

& [CausalOrderModel] is clock neutral
  + relation endpoints are FirstAcquisition.Completion and SecondAcquisition.Start
  + relation predicate is strictly_precedes
  + exactly one directed edge exists for the selected evidence construction
  + inverse or cyclic order is invalid
  + no clock domain, numeric tick, duration, or read method is selected
  + later representation must prove the relation rather than infer it from names

& [CommonScopeModel] is a complete product
  + CandidateRootReference
  + StrongRootIdentity
  + RootVolumeGuidPath
  + ScannerProfile
  + MachineAndTopologyFormsProfiles
  + OrderedObservationEncodingProfile
  + CompleteScanLimits
  + ClosedPolicyDigest
  + PredecessorAdmissionIdentity
  + ReconciliationComparisonScope
  + scope equality means every product coordinate exists and compares exactly
  + no omitted coordinate is default, wildcard, or irrelevant

& [CarrierModel] preserves typed ancestry
  + FirstInventoryCarrier and SecondInventoryCarrier are role-distinct
  + each is current-valid and complete under its own lineage
  + FirstOrderedDigestCarrier derives only from FirstInventoryCarrier
  + SecondOrderedDigestCarrier derives only from SecondInventoryCarrier
  + canonical digest bytes are values inside carriers, not carrier identities
  + rederivation must validate complete carrier ancestry before comparison

& [ReconciliationModel] is subordinate and current
  + consumes exactly two complete ordered digest carriers
  + validates exact current reconciliation profile and common scope
  + independently rederives left then right according to current pure authority
  + releases Equal or Different with retained positional lineage
  + later binding maps acquisition roles to operand roles explicitly without treating operand position as causal proof
  + Equal is one conjunct of evidence derivation
  + Different terminates evidence derivation without physical-state inference

& [EvidenceConstructionModel] is one conjunction
  + FirstAcquisition exists and is complete
  + SecondAcquisition exists and is complete
  + acquisition identities differ
  + FirstCompletion strictly precedes SecondStart
  + CommonScope is complete and equal
  + both independent carrier lineages are complete and current-valid
  + current ReconciliationResult is Equal
  + future issuer authority admits the conjunction
  + only then may consistency_evidence be NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual as an issued claim

& [ReceiptFormModel] remains current and pure
  + receipt 0.3 contains one consistency_evidence label
  + pure validation checks current profile and internal field relations
  + no acquisition identity, lineage graph, causal edge, reconciliation proof, or issuer identity is embedded by this revision
  + valid form cardinality remains independent from evidence-support cardinality
  + OsSnapshotProven remains form-inadmissible under current receipt validation

& [IssuanceModel] is required but absent
  + future IssuanceProof binds evidence construction to exact receipt bytes and issuer authority
  + it also binds predecessor, root, policy, scanner, nonce, inventory, counts, issue, and freshness claims
  + successful issuance releases one authoritative receipt plus proof only under later source
  + failed issuance releases no authoritative partial receipt
  + no public constructor, serde operation, validator, or SJS artifact is an issuance operation

& [ConsumptionModel] is deferred
  + future consumer verifies replacement formation, issuer, evidence lineage, receipt integrity, freshness, exact scope, and single use
  + consumer state is not held by the form or issuer
  + admission and mutation work-packet construction occur only after consumer success under M2E
  + this revision contains zero consumer states or transitions

& [Cardinality] is exact
  + one formation revision source
  + one prior formation signature and at most one selected replacement signature
  + two acquisition identities in two distinct causal roles
  + two complete acquisition lineages
  + one causal order edge
  + one complete common-scope relation
  + two inventory carriers and two ordered digest carriers
  + one reconciliation result
  + one selected evidence grade
  + one receipt claim field
  + zero runtime records, issuers, consumers, ledgers, fixtures, or effects in this slice

& [OwnershipModel] is authority layered
  + source owns intended meaning
  + SJS artifacts own derived governance records
  + future producer owns physical acquisition events and lineages
  + pure modules own only supplied derivation results
  + future issuer owns evidence-to-receipt binding act
  + future consumer owns acceptance state
  + no owner can transfer authority merely by serializing another owner's data

& [ValidationObligations] are staged
  + governance validation checks hashes, source roles, constraints, inheritance, and signature lineage
  + future M2C validation checks acquisition identity, completeness, order, scope, carriers, and reconciliation
  + pure receipt validation checks representation only
  + future issuance validation checks issuer authority and complete binding
  + future consumption validation checks freshness, single use, and operational policy
  + no earlier validation substitutes for a later stage

& [FailureModel] is atomic
  + GovernanceFault for source, predecessor, constraint, inheritance, or signature failure
  + AcquisitionFault for absent, unauthorized, incomplete, duplicate, or malformed future event
  + OrderFault for absent, inverse, cyclic, ambiguous, or unproven causal order
  + ScopeFault for absent or unequal coordinate
  + CarrierFault for incomplete, stale, malformed, or non-current lineage
  + ReconciliationFault for current pure validation failure
  + DifferentDisposition for valid unequal commitments
  + IssuanceFault for absent authority or incomplete binding
  + this slice implements none of these runtime faults and defines only conceptual categories for later authority

& [StateModel] is split
  + governance states progress from source_preserved to replacement_formation_signed
  + future acquisition states progress independently from requested to complete or fault
  + future evidence state progresses only after both complete acquisitions and all conjuncts
  + receipt form state progresses independently from encoded to structurally_valid or fault
  + issuance state and consumption state remain separate future machines
  + no transition crosses machines without an explicit authority-bearing relation

& [VersionAndCompatibilityModel] is prospective
  + prior formation bytes and signature remain historical
  + replacement canonical does not mutate prior artifacts
  + current forms and lower carrier signatures are dependencies and remain governing in their scopes
  + scanner profile remains unchanged only for unchanged observation behavior
  + any later runtime representation or scanner behavior change receives new source and profile decision
  + no runtime migration exists because no scanner issuer or consumer exists

& [ResourceModel] is document bounded
  + current slice adds only finite SOP records and relation tables
  + no collection, buffer, traversal, digest, thread, process, database row, persistent record, or memory budget is added to production
  + later acquisition resource limits remain inherited prospective constraints

& [EffectModel] is empty
  + no production or Cargo file changes
  + no unsafe or external dependency
  + no platform, filesystem, handle, pointer, clock, random, process, network, persistence, Git runtime, model, tool, fixture, scan, acquisition, receipt issuance, consumption, mutation, seal, test execution, cleanup, promotion, neural, distributed, or FPGA operation

& [DataQualityRules] are testable at formation level
  + every source and predecessor hash matches
  + all ten requirements and twenty-four constraints map completely
  + vocabulary and profiles are exact
  + conceptual cardinalities and relation directions are exact
  + forbidden inference graph has no promotion path
  + inherited scanner formation families are complete
  + repository production and Cargo deltas remain zero
  + replacement signature is absent until every SJS artifact is content-addressed

& [DataRisks] are controlled
  + authority collapse is controlled by separate identities and state machines
  + provenance laundering is controlled by complete conjunctive evidence construction
  + temporal inflation is controlled by causal-role semantics and non-atomic nonclaims
  + scope laundering is controlled by complete product equality
  + digest laundering is controlled by full carrier ancestry
  + receipt self-authorization is controlled by issuance separation
  + current-world inflation is controlled by exact evidence boundary
  + implementation creep is controlled by zero runtime ownership and effects

& [DataDesignGate] passes
  + identities, ownership, cardinality, ordering, representation, relations, states, versioning, and failure categories are explicit
  + runtime representation is deliberately deferred without leaving semantic ambiguity
  + every C01 through C24 constraint reapplies without collision
  + all seven exhaustion folds converge on this model
  + [unresolved_data_question] is none inside the selected formation revision
  + [source_revision_required] is false
  + [implementation_authority] is absent
  + [execution_authority] is absent
  + [physical_authority] is absent
